    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Uber Technologies, Inc operates a platform that, according to its website, lets users earn money, order food, commute, get rides, and manage business travel. The site describes Uber for Business as providing organizations with more control, deeper insights, and features built for enterprise users, including a dashboard for business travel and meal programs. It also advertises a promotional offer for new Uber Eats delivery people: eligible participants may earn $150 for every 15 unique deliveries completed within 14 days of signing up with Uber Eats, up to a maximum reward of $450, with the site noting this is not a guarantee of future earnings.\n\nThe available material does not mention artificial intelligence, and no AI products or MCP servers are listed for the company.\n\nUber Technologies, Inc is a for-profit public company headquartered in San Francisco, CA, trading under the ticker UBER. Its SEC Central Index Key is 0001543151. Public records list 281 legal matters in California associated with the company. No individual court cases are listed in the available material.",
